:"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman","html_url":"https://github.com/romgerman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-09T15:41:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-09T17:01:55Z","body":"> Exporting inner classes is [not supported](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/scripting/resources.html#creating-your-own-resources)\n\nHow could it be not supported and half-working at the same time?\n1. It serializes the inner resource just fine\n2. It cannot load the inner resource - the resource is just an empty resource when it loads it\n3. Godot editor breaks the `.tres` file but it should not even touch it if the resource was not modified\n\nI see multiple problems here. The main problem is 3rd point. Why does it re-save the resource when it cannot even show the exported properties which means the resource cannot be edited which means it should not touch it at all. It's again the problem of Godot's editor trying to act smart when it shouldn't act at all.\n\n(I may be wrong and Godot's editor indeed needs to rewrite the Resource data. But I don't know why)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4024717101/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]